WEBVTT

00:03:06.090 --> 00:03:09.250
Who am I? You sure you want to know?

00:03:09.450 --> 00:03:12.710
The story of my life
is not for the faint of heart.

00:03:12.870 --> 00:03:15.500
If somebody said
it was a happy little tale...

00:03:15.710 --> 00:03:20.160
... if somebody told you I was just an
average guy, not a care in the world...

00:03:20.330 --> 00:03:22.120
... somebody lied.

00:03:23.000 --> 00:03:26.580
But let me assure you, this,
like any story worth telling...

00:03:26.740 --> 00:03:28.160
... is all about a girl.

00:03:29.040 --> 00:03:33.500
That girl. The girl next door.
Mary Jane Watson.

00:03:33.670 --> 00:03:36.740
The woman I've loved
since before I liked girls.

00:03:36.910 --> 00:03:39.580
I'd like to tell you that's me
next to her.

00:03:39.750 --> 00:03:41.750
Aw, heck, I'd even take him.

00:03:43.170 --> 00:03:45.660
Hey! Stop the bus!

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:47.830
That's me.

00:03:48.040 --> 00:03:49.910
Tell him to stop! Please!

00:03:50.120 --> 00:03:51.330
Stop!

00:03:51.540 --> 00:03:53.740
Hey! Stop the bus!

00:03:53.910 --> 00:03:56.990
Stop! He's been chasing us
since Woodhaven.

00:03:57.160 --> 00:03:58.410
Catch a cab, Parker!

00:04:02.860 --> 00:04:05.660
Thank you. I'm sorry I'm late.

00:04:11.080 --> 00:04:12.360
What a geek!

00:04:13.030 --> 00:04:17.240
- Don't even think about it.
- You're so lame, Parker.

00:04:17.410 --> 00:04:19.000
Would you date him?

00:04:36.870 --> 00:04:39.080
Midtown High seniors.

00:04:39.250 --> 00:04:42.950
No wandering. Proceed direct...
Knock it off.

00:04:43.240 --> 00:04:46.700
Remember, it is a privilege
to be here.

00:04:47.080 --> 00:04:50.320
We're guests of Columbia University's
Science Department.

00:04:50.530 --> 00:04:52.740
So behave accordingly.

00:04:52.910 --> 00:04:55.950
Let's not have a repeat
of our trip to the planetarium.

00:04:56.160 --> 00:04:57.790
Come on, stay together.

00:04:57.940 --> 00:05:00.860
Proceed up the steps
and into the building.

00:05:02.030 --> 00:05:05.070
- Where were you?
- Checking out the library.

00:05:05.240 --> 00:05:07.780
- Looking at the books.
- Yeah, right.

00:05:09.530 --> 00:05:13.360
- Can we drive around the corner?
- Why?

00:05:13.570 --> 00:05:15.370
The entrance is right there.

00:05:15.530 --> 00:05:19.240
Dad, this is public school.
I can't show up in a Rolls.

00:05:19.440 --> 00:05:21.780
I should trade my car for a Jetta...

00:05:21.950 --> 00:05:24.740
...because you flunked out
of private school?

00:05:25.030 --> 00:05:28.070
- It wasn't for me.
- Of course it was.

00:05:28.730 --> 00:05:33.070
- Don't ever be ashamed of who you are.
- I'm not ashamed of who I am.

00:05:33.280 --> 00:05:34.570
It's just...

00:05:34.740 --> 00:05:36.190
Just what, Harry?

00:05:36.400 --> 00:05:37.900
Forget it.

00:05:40.900 --> 00:05:42.240
Pete!

00:05:42.660 --> 00:05:45.150
- Hi, Harry.
- Hey, man. What's up?

00:05:46.020 --> 00:05:48.230
- Won't you be needing this?
- Thanks.

00:05:49.190 --> 00:05:53.160
- This is my father, Norman Osborn.
- I've heard so much about you.

00:05:53.360 --> 00:05:56.820
- It's an honor, sir.
- Harry says you're a science whiz.

00:05:57.070 --> 00:05:59.900
I'm something of a scientist myself.

00:06:00.070 --> 00:06:03.230
I read your research
on nanotechnology. Brilliant.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:06.440
- You understood it?
- Yes, I wrote a paper on it.

00:06:06.650 --> 00:06:09.940
Impressive.
Your parents must be very proud.

00:06:10.110 --> 00:06:14.650
- I live with my aunt and uncle.
- Hey, you two! Let's move!

00:06:14.810 --> 00:06:18.480
- Nice to meet you.
- Hope to see you again.

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:24.310
- He doesn't seem so bad.
- Not if you're a genius.

00:06:24.480 --> 00:06:26.440
I think he wants to adopt you.

00:06:26.610 --> 00:06:27.230
There are over 32,000 known species
of spider in the world.

00:06:27.230 --> 00:06:31.310
There are over 32,000 known species
of spider in the world.

00:06:31.520 --> 00:06:35.310
They're in the order Araneae,
divided into three suborders.

00:06:35.520 --> 00:06:36.610
That's amazing!

00:06:36.770 --> 00:06:40.690
This is the most advanced electron
microscope on the East Coast.

00:06:41.020 --> 00:06:43.060
It's unreal.

00:06:43.230 --> 00:06:46.020
Arachnids from all three
groups possess...

00:06:46.230 --> 00:06:49.730
...varying strengths
to help them search for food.

00:06:49.930 --> 00:06:54.150
For example, the Delena spider,
family Sparassidae...

00:06:54.310 --> 00:06:58.480
...has the ability to jump
to catch its prey.

00:06:58.640 --> 00:07:00.390
For the school paper?

00:07:04.900 --> 00:07:09.890
Next, we have the net web spider,
family Filistatidae...

00:07:10.100 --> 00:07:11.980
...genus Kukulcania.

00:07:12.230 --> 00:07:16.570
Spins a funnel- shaped web whose
strands have a tensile strength...

00:07:16.770 --> 00:07:22.020
...proportionately equal to
the high-tension wires used in bridges.

00:07:22.480 --> 00:07:24.150
- Leave him alone.
- Or what?

00:07:24.310 --> 00:07:27.310
Or his father will fire your father.

00:07:27.720 --> 00:07:30.060
What's Daddy gonna do? Sue me?

00:07:30.230 --> 00:07:32.730
What is going on?

00:07:32.900 --> 00:07:35.970
The next person who talks
will fail this course.

00:07:36.180 --> 00:07:38.180
- This spider...
- Let's go.

00:07:38.350 --> 00:07:42.520
...hunts using reflexes with
nerve- conduction velocity so fast...

00:07:42.730 --> 00:07:46.220
...that some researchers believe
it borders on precognition.

00:07:46.390 --> 00:07:48.560
- An early awareness of danger.
- Jerks.

00:07:48.770 --> 00:07:50.520
A spider- sense.

00:07:51.140 --> 00:07:52.810
Hey, look at that spider.

00:07:52.980 --> 00:07:57.390
Some spiders change colors
to blend into their environment.

00:07:57.640 --> 00:07:59.560
It's a defense mechanism.

00:07:59.730 --> 00:08:03.020
Peter, what makes you think
I'd want to know that?

00:08:03.190 --> 00:08:04.390
Who wouldn't?

00:08:04.550 --> 00:08:08.390
Over five painstaking years,
Columbia's research facility...

00:08:08.560 --> 00:08:12.930
- You gonna talk to her now?
- Oh, no. Come on. You talk to her.

00:08:13.140 --> 00:08:17.890
With these DNA blueprints, we have
begun what was once thought impossible.

00:08:18.100 --> 00:08:21.770
- Disgusting.
- Yeah, hateful little things.

00:08:21.980 --> 00:08:23.340
I love them!

00:08:23.890 --> 00:08:25.560
Yeah, me too.

00:08:26.510 --> 00:08:30.390
You know, spiders can change
their color...

00:08:30.560 --> 00:08:34.390
...to blend into their environment.
- Really?

00:08:34.550 --> 00:08:38.680
- Yeah, it's a defense mechanism.
- Cool.

00:08:38.890 --> 00:08:42.260
- Transfer RNA
to encode an entirely new genome...

00:08:42.430 --> 00:08:45.560
...combining the genetic
information from all three...

00:08:45.720 --> 00:08:50.380
...into these 15 genetically
designed super- spiders.

00:08:50.550 --> 00:08:52.050
There's 14.

00:08:52.510 --> 00:08:53.890
I beg your pardon?

00:08:54.050 --> 00:08:56.600
- One's missing.
- Yeah.

00:08:59.510 --> 00:09:02.140
I guess the researchers
are working on that one.

00:09:02.640 --> 00:09:07.350
Do you know that this is the largest
electron microscope on the East Coast?

00:09:07.520 --> 00:09:11.590
You were talking throughout
that woman's entire presentation.

00:09:11.760 --> 00:09:13.510
Let's talk about listening.

00:09:17.600 --> 00:09:20.340
I don't know what it's like
at those fancy private schools...

00:09:20.340 --> 00:09:21.680
I don't know what it's like
at those fancy private schools...

00:09:21.880 --> 00:09:23.760
...but at Midtown High...

00:09:32.220 --> 00:09:35.970
Could I take your picture?
I need one with a student in it.

00:09:36.140 --> 00:09:37.590
- Sure.
- Great.

00:09:37.800 --> 00:09:40.090
Where do you want me?
Over here?

00:09:40.300 --> 00:09:41.630
Yeah, that's great.

00:09:42.050 --> 00:09:43.720
Don't make me look ugly.

00:09:44.100 --> 00:09:45.920
That's impossible.

00:09:53.180 --> 00:09:54.430
Perfect.

00:10:02.180 --> 00:10:03.720
- Is that good?
- Great.

00:10:09.260 --> 00:10:10.630
That's great.

00:10:16.210 --> 00:10:18.210
M.J., let's go!

00:10:19.760 --> 00:10:22.340
Wait. Thanks!

00:10:35.800 --> 00:10:38.550
Parker, let's do it.

00:10:55.250 --> 00:10:58.720
We've solved the horizon glide
and the balance issues.

00:10:58.880 --> 00:11:01.420
I've already seen the glider.

00:11:01.830 --> 00:11:03.880
That's not what I'm here for.

00:11:04.090 --> 00:11:06.750
General Slocum, good to see you again.

00:11:07.590 --> 00:11:09.750
Mr. Balkan, Mr. Fargas.

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.830
- Norman.
- Mr. Osborn.

00:11:12.000 --> 00:11:15.550
Always a pleasure to have
our board of directors visit.

00:11:15.750 --> 00:11:19.160
I want the report on human
performance enhancers.

00:11:19.330 --> 00:11:23.840
We tried vapor inhalation with rats.
Their strength increased by 800%.

00:11:24.000 --> 00:11:25.880
- Excellent.
- Any side effects?

00:11:26.050 --> 00:11:27.130
Once.

00:11:27.300 --> 00:11:29.960
All the tests since
have been successful.

00:11:30.120 --> 00:11:33.880
In the trial that went wrong,
what were the side effects?

00:11:34.040 --> 00:11:36.380
Violence, aggression...

00:11:37.050 --> 00:11:38.290
...and insanity.

00:11:38.450 --> 00:11:41.210
- What do you recommend?
- That was only one test.

00:11:41.460 --> 00:11:45.300
Except for Dr. Stromm,
our staff certifies the product...

00:11:45.460 --> 00:11:48.370
...ready for human testing.
- Dr. Stromm?

00:11:49.710 --> 00:11:53.380
We need to take the whole line
back to formula.

00:11:54.630 --> 00:11:57.040
- Back to formula?
- Dr. Osborn.

00:11:58.200 --> 00:12:00.040
I'll be frank with you.

00:12:00.290 --> 00:12:05.120
I never supported your program. We
have my predecessor to thank for that.

00:12:05.290 --> 00:12:08.040
The general has approved
Quest Aerospace...

00:12:08.200 --> 00:12:11.120
...to build a prototype
of their exoskeleton.

00:12:11.460 --> 00:12:15.370
- They test in two weeks.
- And if your performance enhancers...

00:12:15.540 --> 00:12:19.620
...have not had a successful
human trial by that date...

00:12:19.870 --> 00:12:24.240
...l'm gonna pull your funding.
I'm going to give it to them.

00:12:26.040 --> 00:12:27.700
Gentlemen. Ladies.

00:12:32.780 --> 00:12:38.200
And the Lord said, "Let there be light."
And voilÃ ! There is light.

00:12:38.460 --> 00:12:40.540
Forty soft, glowing watts of it.

00:12:40.710 --> 00:12:45.540
Good boy. God will be thrilled.
Just don't fall on your ass.

00:12:45.870 --> 00:12:48.290
I'm already on my ass, May.

00:12:48.460 --> 00:12:52.950
When the plant's senior electrician
is laid off after 35 years...

00:12:53.120 --> 00:12:55.830
...what would you call it?
I am on my ass.

00:12:56.040 --> 00:12:58.370
Hand me that dish. The green one.

00:12:58.620 --> 00:13:01.360
The corporation is downsizing
the people...

00:13:01.820 --> 00:13:03.700
...and upsizing their profits.

00:13:03.950 --> 00:13:06.870
Oh, Ben, you'll get another job
somewhere.

00:13:07.870 --> 00:13:10.780
Well, let's look
in the paper and see.

00:13:11.910 --> 00:13:14.700
There are the want ads.
What do we got here?

00:13:14.870 --> 00:13:16.490
Computer...

00:13:16.700 --> 00:13:20.450
Computer salesman, computer engineer,
computer analyst.

00:13:20.610 --> 00:13:24.370
My Lord, even the computers
need analysts these days.

00:13:24.660 --> 00:13:29.950
I'm 68. I'm too old for computers, and
besides, I have a family to provide for.

00:13:30.160 --> 00:13:33.030
I love you. And Peter loves you.

00:13:33.280 --> 00:13:36.540
You're the most responsible man
I've ever known.

00:13:36.790 --> 00:13:41.200
We've been down-and-out before.
But somehow, we survive.

00:13:42.320 --> 00:13:46.620
Hi, sweetie. You're just...
Just in time for dinner.

00:13:46.830 --> 00:13:49.360
How you doing? How was the field trip?

00:13:49.530 --> 00:13:52.370
I don't feel well.
I'm gonna go to sleep.

00:13:52.530 --> 00:13:55.040
- You won't have a bite?
- Had a bite.

00:13:55.200 --> 00:13:57.610
Did you get some pictures, Peter?

00:13:58.450 --> 00:14:01.280
I gotta crash. Everything's fine.

00:14:02.700 --> 00:14:04.280
What's that all about?

00:14:25.530 --> 00:14:27.740
In this recombination lab...

00:14:27.900 --> 00:14:32.530
... we use synthesized transfer RNA
to encode an entirely new genome...

00:14:32.740 --> 00:14:35.780
... combining the genetic
information from all three...

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:40.780
... into these 15 genetically
designed super-spiders.

00:14:55.230 --> 00:14:59.200
Dr. Osborn, please.
The performance enhancers aren't ready.

00:14:59.360 --> 00:15:02.690
The data just doesn't justify
this test.

00:15:02.860 --> 00:15:06.530
Now, I'm asking you for the last time.
We can't do this.

00:15:06.690 --> 00:15:08.900
Don't be a coward.

00:15:09.360 --> 00:15:11.940
Risks are part of laboratory science.

00:15:12.150 --> 00:15:15.860
Let me reschedule,
with a medical staff and a volunteer.

00:15:16.070 --> 00:15:18.530
- Just give me two weeks.
- Two weeks?

00:15:18.700 --> 00:15:23.190
In two weeks? We'll have lost the contract
to Quest and OSCORP will be dead.

00:15:23.360 --> 00:15:26.110
Sometimes you gotta
do things yourself.

00:15:26.280 --> 00:15:28.950
- Get me the Promachloraperazine.
- For what?

00:15:29.100 --> 00:15:32.860
It begins catalyzation when the vapor
hits the bloodstream.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:37.440
40,000 years of evolution...

00:15:37.610 --> 00:15:41.350
...and we've barely tapped
the vastness of human potential.

00:15:55.190 --> 00:15:56.530
Oh, that's cold.

00:16:54.930 --> 00:16:56.180
Norman?

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:01.970
Norman!

00:17:12.680 --> 00:17:14.010
Oh, my God.

00:17:15.520 --> 00:17:16.930
Oh, my God!

00:17:19.600 --> 00:17:21.430
Oh, my God! Norman!

00:17:37.810 --> 00:17:39.430
Back to formula?

00:18:14.010 --> 00:18:15.520
Weird.

00:18:26.420 --> 00:18:27.800
- Peter?
- Yeah?

00:18:28.010 --> 00:18:29.760
Are you all right?

00:18:31.680 --> 00:18:33.310
I'm fine.

00:18:33.890 --> 00:18:37.260
- Any better this morning? Any change?
- Change?

00:18:38.260 --> 00:18:40.180
Yep. Big change.

00:18:40.340 --> 00:18:44.340
- Well, hurry up. You'll be late.
- Right.

00:19:02.710 --> 00:19:04.090
Okay.

00:19:08.800 --> 00:19:12.590
- Goodness me!
- Jeez. I thought you were sick.

00:19:13.130 --> 00:19:14.460
- I got better.
- See?

00:19:14.630 --> 00:19:18.010
- Bye, guys.
- Have you got your lunch money?

00:19:18.180 --> 00:19:21.840
Don't forget, we're painting
the kitchen after school.

00:19:22.000 --> 00:19:24.800
Sure, Uncle Ben.
Don't start without me.

00:19:25.010 --> 00:19:27.090
And don't start up with me.

00:19:28.680 --> 00:19:32.340
Teenagers. Raging hormones.
They never change.

00:19:33.300 --> 00:19:37.010
You're trash!
You're always gonna be trash!

00:19:37.170 --> 00:19:40.750
- I have to go to school.
- Who's stopping you?

00:19:58.130 --> 00:19:59.790
Hi, M.J.

00:20:00.670 --> 00:20:02.170
Hey, M.J.

00:20:02.420 --> 00:20:06.970
I don't know if you realize this, but
we've been neighbors since I was 6.

00:20:07.130 --> 00:20:10.460
And I was wondering
if we could get together sometime?

00:20:10.670 --> 00:20:11.960
I got the car. Hop in.

00:20:12.130 --> 00:20:15.010
Do something fun?
Or, I don't know.

00:20:15.210 --> 00:20:19.040
I thought it'd be time
to get to know each other.

00:20:19.290 --> 00:20:20.540
Or not.

00:20:26.010 --> 00:20:28.710
Sorry, Parker, the bus is full!

00:20:30.250 --> 00:20:32.790
- Stop the bus!
- Catch a cab!

00:20:33.210 --> 00:20:34.840
Tell him to stop.

00:20:35.500 --> 00:20:37.500
- Check him out!
- Dork!

00:20:59.960 --> 00:21:01.210
Dad!

00:21:01.670 --> 00:21:03.540
Dad, are you all right?

00:21:04.370 --> 00:21:05.660
Harry.

00:21:09.000 --> 00:21:11.000
What are you doing on the floor?

00:21:11.170 --> 00:21:12.500
I don't know.

00:21:13.330 --> 00:21:15.660
Have you been there all night?

00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:18.920
Last night I was...

00:21:21.250 --> 00:21:22.490
What?

00:21:23.740 --> 00:21:26.160
- I don't remember.
- Mr. Osborn?

00:21:26.370 --> 00:21:28.040
Sir, I asked her to wait.

00:21:28.210 --> 00:21:32.530
- My father's not feeling well...
- Mr. Osborn, Dr. Stromm is dead.

00:21:32.700 --> 00:21:33.740
What?

00:21:33.910 --> 00:21:37.500
They found his body in the lab.
He's been murdered, sir.

00:21:37.660 --> 00:21:41.030
- What?
- And the flight suit and the glider...

00:21:41.200 --> 00:21:43.200
- What about it?
- Stolen, sir.

00:22:08.120 --> 00:22:10.870
Wow! Great reflexes!

00:22:11.740 --> 00:22:13.910
- Thanks.
- No problem.

00:22:15.000 --> 00:22:18.910
Hey, you have blue eyes.
I didn't notice without your glasses.

00:22:19.660 --> 00:22:21.330
You just get contacts?

00:22:28.070 --> 00:22:30.240
Well, see you.

00:23:11.990 --> 00:23:15.490
- What happened?
- He's freaking weird.

00:23:15.940 --> 00:23:17.320
Did you see that?

00:23:18.910 --> 00:23:20.570
Parker?

00:23:52.400 --> 00:23:54.820
- It's a fight!
- Think you're funny?

00:23:54.990 --> 00:23:57.990
- It was an accident.
- So is my breaking your teeth.

00:23:58.200 --> 00:24:00.900
- Flash, stop.
- I don't want to fight you.

00:24:01.070 --> 00:24:04.490
- I wouldn't want to fight me neither.
- Kick his ass.

00:24:23.360 --> 00:24:24.690
Help him, Harry.

00:24:29.650 --> 00:24:31.150
How'd he do that?

00:24:32.230 --> 00:24:33.480
Which one?

00:24:33.650 --> 00:24:35.030
He's all yours, man.

00:24:50.520 --> 00:24:52.230
Flash, get up!

00:24:53.860 --> 00:24:56.980
Jesus, Parker, you are a freak.

00:24:58.900 --> 00:25:00.400
That was amazing.

00:25:01.320 --> 00:25:03.320
I'm out of here. Come on.

00:26:48.390 --> 00:26:49.430
Go, web!

00:26:51.010 --> 00:26:52.640
Fly.

00:26:54.230 --> 00:26:56.300
Up, up and away, web.

00:26:57.890 --> 00:26:59.300
Shazam!

00:26:59.890 --> 00:27:01.140
Go! Go!

00:27:01.390 --> 00:27:03.140
Go, web, go!

00:27:36.220 --> 00:27:37.970
Tallyho.

00:28:21.840 --> 00:28:24.420
- Is she back with the beer yet?
- What?

00:28:24.630 --> 00:28:25.880
Bring me some beer.

00:28:26.090 --> 00:28:28.640
- Get up off your ass.
- I paid for beer...

00:28:28.790 --> 00:28:30.290
- Stop yelling.
- Stop it!

00:28:30.460 --> 00:28:32.800
You're as stupid as your mother.

00:28:34.720 --> 00:28:37.260
Where's she going?
Where you going?

00:28:38.330 --> 00:28:41.670
The dishes aren't done.
Somebody's gotta do dishes.

00:28:41.880 --> 00:28:45.170
- Why don't you do them?
- Get in here and do the dishes.

00:28:45.380 --> 00:28:49.500
- You do them. They're yours, anyway.
- I'm going out!

00:28:49.710 --> 00:28:52.210
- Were you listening to that?
- No.

00:28:52.550 --> 00:28:55.800
Well, I heard, but I was
just taking out the trash.

00:28:55.970 --> 00:28:58.710
I guess you can always hear us.

00:28:58.880 --> 00:29:01.170
Everybody shouts.

00:29:01.630 --> 00:29:03.760
Your aunt and uncle don't.

00:29:03.920 --> 00:29:06.460
Oh, they can scream
pretty good sometimes.

00:29:07.880 --> 00:29:12.090
Listen, M.J., about today
at school with Flash...

00:29:12.340 --> 00:29:13.960
You really freaked us out.

00:29:14.170 --> 00:29:16.420
I'm sorry. Is he okay?

00:29:16.710 --> 00:29:20.670
He's just happy you didn't give him
a black eye for graduation.

00:29:23.760 --> 00:29:26.960
So where are you going
after you graduate?

00:29:31.710 --> 00:29:34.000
I wanna move into the city.

00:29:34.910 --> 00:29:39.710
And hopefully, get a job
as a photographer.

00:29:39.880 --> 00:29:42.710
Work my way through college.

00:29:43.700 --> 00:29:45.040
What about you?

00:29:45.210 --> 00:29:47.210
Headed for the city too.

00:29:47.920 --> 00:29:50.170
Can't wait to get out of here.

00:29:51.340 --> 00:29:52.830
I wanna...

00:29:54.080 --> 00:29:55.580
What?

00:29:58.420 --> 00:30:00.670
No, come on. Try me.

00:30:01.590 --> 00:30:03.080
I wanna...

00:30:04.210 --> 00:30:05.540
...act...

00:30:06.710 --> 00:30:08.210
...on-stage.

00:30:08.790 --> 00:30:10.630
Really?

00:30:10.990 --> 00:30:13.160
Oh, that's perfect.

00:30:13.450 --> 00:30:16.000
You were awesome
in all the school plays.

00:30:16.330 --> 00:30:18.170
- Really?
- Yeah.

00:30:18.790 --> 00:30:21.790
I cried like a baby
when you played Cinderella.

00:30:22.290 --> 00:30:24.500
Peter, that was first grade.

00:30:25.000 --> 00:30:26.500
Well...

00:30:27.040 --> 00:30:28.540
...even so.

00:30:29.530 --> 00:30:31.450
Sometimes...

00:30:32.290 --> 00:30:33.960
...you know people.

00:30:35.120 --> 00:30:38.710
You can just see what's coming.

00:30:41.790 --> 00:30:44.540
What do you see coming for you?

00:30:47.120 --> 00:30:48.780
I don't know.

00:30:51.120 --> 00:30:55.790
Whatever it is, it's something
I never felt before.

00:30:59.370 --> 00:31:02.290
And what for me?

00:31:02.450 --> 00:31:03.790
For you?

00:31:05.210 --> 00:31:07.950
You're gonna light up Broadway.

00:31:09.450 --> 00:31:10.790
You know...

00:31:15.160 --> 00:31:17.780
...you're taller than you look.

00:31:17.950 --> 00:31:19.490
I hunch.

00:31:21.740 --> 00:31:23.250
Don't.

00:31:26.780 --> 00:31:30.330
Hey, M.J.! Come take a ride
in my new birthday present.

00:31:31.410 --> 00:31:32.700
Come on.

00:31:33.790 --> 00:31:35.110
I gotta go.

00:31:35.950 --> 00:31:37.110
Bye.

00:31:37.780 --> 00:31:40.450
- Oh, my God, it's gorgeous!
- Yeah, right.

00:31:40.620 --> 00:31:42.620
- Look at it!
- Hop in.

00:31:42.790 --> 00:31:45.030
Oh, my God. What a cool car!

00:31:45.280 --> 00:31:46.860
Pretty tight, huh?

00:31:47.280 --> 00:31:51.620
Wait till you hear the sound system.
Hey, don't scratch the leather.

00:31:53.360 --> 00:31:54.610
Cool car.

00:33:27.230 --> 00:33:29.270
What's going on in there?

00:33:29.480 --> 00:33:32.110
I'm exercising.
I'm not dressed, Aunt May.

00:33:32.280 --> 00:33:35.940
Well, you're acting
so strangely, Peter.

00:33:36.230 --> 00:33:38.310
Okay. Thanks.

00:34:09.110 --> 00:34:12.430
Something's wrong.
Maybe he's too embarrassed to tell me.

00:34:12.600 --> 00:34:15.270
Maybe I'm too embarrassed to ask him.

00:34:16.060 --> 00:34:18.110
I just don't know anymore.

00:34:18.520 --> 00:34:21.070
I'm going to the library.
See you later.

00:34:21.280 --> 00:34:24.640
- Wait. I'll drive you there.
- I'll take the train.

00:34:24.810 --> 00:34:28.060
No, I need the exercise.
Go on. Go, go.

00:34:39.110 --> 00:34:42.560
- Thanks for the ride, Uncle Ben.
- Wait. We need to talk.

00:34:42.730 --> 00:34:47.110
- We can talk later.
- Well, we can talk now. If you let me.

00:34:47.980 --> 00:34:50.220
What do we have to talk about?
Why now?

00:34:50.390 --> 00:34:54.440
We haven't talked for so long.
May and I don't know who you are.

00:34:54.600 --> 00:34:59.600
You shirk your chores. You have all
those weird experiments in your room.

00:34:59.760 --> 00:35:03.890
- You start fights at school.
- I told you I didn't start that fight.

00:35:04.100 --> 00:35:07.060
- You sure finished it.
- Was I supposed to run away?

00:35:07.270 --> 00:35:10.270
No, you're not supposed
to run away, but...

00:35:10.430 --> 00:35:14.980
You're changing. I went through
exactly the same thing at your age.

00:35:15.190 --> 00:35:17.190
No. Not exactly.

00:35:18.550 --> 00:35:21.270
These are the years
when a man changes...

00:35:21.430 --> 00:35:25.440
...into the man he's gonna become
the rest of his life.

00:35:25.600 --> 00:35:28.680
Just be careful who you change into.

00:35:30.220 --> 00:35:34.730
This guy, Flash Thompson,
he probably deserved what happened.

00:35:35.270 --> 00:35:37.970
But just because you can
beat him up...

00:35:38.430 --> 00:35:40.680
...doesn't give you the right to.

00:35:41.350 --> 00:35:46.590
Remember, with great power
comes great responsibility.

00:35:47.180 --> 00:35:52.180
Are you afraid I'll become a criminal?
Quit worrying about me, okay?

00:35:52.350 --> 00:35:55.760
Something's different.
I'll figure it out. Stop lecturing.

00:35:56.050 --> 00:36:00.270
I don't mean to lecture or preach.
And I know I'm not your father.

00:36:00.430 --> 00:36:03.270
Then stop pretending to be!

00:36:07.350 --> 00:36:08.600
Right.

00:36:11.560 --> 00:36:13.510
I'll pick you up here at 10.

00:36:44.720 --> 00:36:45.220
Bone Saw! Bone Saw! Bone Saw!

00:36:45.220 --> 00:36:47.390
Bone Saw! Bone Saw! Bone Saw!

00:36:47.390 --> 00:36:50.550
Bone Saw! Bone Saw! Bone Saw!

00:36:55.260 --> 00:36:59.300
- One, two, three. That's it!
- Who's the man?

00:37:03.420 --> 00:37:05.640
Ladies and gentlemen...

00:37:05.800 --> 00:37:10.340
...give it up for Bone Saw McGraw.

00:37:13.420 --> 00:37:17.100
For $3000...

00:37:17.260 --> 00:37:20.880
...is there no one here man enough
to stay in the ring...

00:37:21.050 --> 00:37:25.760
...for three minutes
with this titan of testosterone?

00:37:28.340 --> 00:37:30.420
Who?

00:37:30.670 --> 00:37:32.550
I know who.

00:37:32.760 --> 00:37:37.540
The Flying Dutchman!

00:37:37.880 --> 00:37:39.340
Next.

00:37:40.170 --> 00:37:43.470
There's no featherweight
division here. Next.

00:37:43.630 --> 00:37:45.470
No, no. Sign me up.

00:37:45.880 --> 00:37:49.300
Okay. You understand the NYWL
is not responsible...

00:37:49.500 --> 00:37:53.680
...for any injury you may and probably
will sustain in said event?

00:37:53.880 --> 00:37:57.000
And you're participating
under your own free will?

00:37:57.170 --> 00:38:01.210
Down the hall to the ramp.
May God be with you. Next.

00:38:03.800 --> 00:38:06.040
Told you! Told you!

00:38:06.250 --> 00:38:08.040
Winner!

00:38:08.250 --> 00:38:09.460
Next victim!

00:38:11.340 --> 00:38:14.210
Are you ready for more?

00:38:15.330 --> 00:38:18.920
Bone Saw is ready!

00:38:21.340 --> 00:38:26.000
Will the next victim please
enter the arena at this time?

00:38:26.210 --> 00:38:30.920
If he can withstand just three minutes
in the cage with Bone Saw McGraw...

00:38:31.170 --> 00:38:35.540
...the sum of $3000 will be paid to...

00:38:36.420 --> 00:38:39.420
- What's your name, kid?
- The Human Spider.

00:38:40.000 --> 00:38:42.370
The Human Spider? That's it? That's the best you got?

00:38:42.540 --> 00:38:44.670
- Yeah.
- Oh, that sucks.

00:38:44.830 --> 00:38:49.340
The sum of $3000 will be paid to...

00:38:49.500 --> 00:38:52.750
...the terrifying, the deadly...

00:38:53.000 --> 00:38:56.210
...the amazing Spider-Man!

00:38:58.590 --> 00:39:01.200
- My name's, "The Human Spider."
- Get out there.

00:39:01.370 --> 00:39:04.420
- No, he got my name wrong.
- Get out there, you moron!

00:39:06.920 --> 00:39:09.450
Bone Saw will eat you up
and spit you out, little man.

00:39:09.700 --> 00:39:11.750
I hope you brought your mommy with you.

00:39:11.910 --> 00:39:16.170
- We'll break you!
- You'll need someone to cry to.

00:39:16.710 --> 00:39:21.830
I'm gonna rip all eight of your
feeble legs off one by one.

00:39:22.330 --> 00:39:24.370
Oh, my God!

00:39:24.580 --> 00:39:26.210
Oh, my legs!

00:39:26.380 --> 00:39:28.990
Oh, God. I can't feel my legs.

00:39:29.160 --> 00:39:31.160
Kill! Kill! Kill!

00:39:39.410 --> 00:39:40.910
Cage! Cage! Cage!

00:39:41.080 --> 00:39:42.290
Cage!

00:39:51.620 --> 00:39:53.080
Hello? Guys?

00:39:54.120 --> 00:39:59.080
Will the guards please lock
the cage doors at this time?

00:39:59.790 --> 00:40:04.080
This is some kind of mistake.
I didn't sign up for a cage match!

00:40:05.240 --> 00:40:07.740
Hey! Unlock the thing! Take the chain off!

00:40:07.950 --> 00:40:09.740
Hey, freak show!

00:40:09.950 --> 00:40:12.580
You're going nowhere.

00:40:12.750 --> 00:40:15.120
I got you for three minutes.

00:40:15.280 --> 00:40:17.580
Three minutes of playtime.

00:40:24.200 --> 00:40:27.660
- What are you doing up there?
- Staying away from you.

00:40:27.870 --> 00:40:31.910
That's a cute outfit.
Did your husband give it to you?

00:40:37.580 --> 00:40:39.120
Finish him off!

00:40:46.280 --> 00:40:47.830
Smash him!

00:40:54.990 --> 00:40:56.740
- Hit him!
- Harder!

00:40:58.740 --> 00:41:01.070
Kick his spider ass!

00:41:03.070 --> 00:41:04.240
Hit him!

00:41:17.660 --> 00:41:19.440
One, two, three!

00:41:19.650 --> 00:41:22.450
That's it! That's it!
Winner!

00:41:22.610 --> 00:41:27.700
Ladies and gentlemen, give it up
for the new champion, Spider-Man!

00:41:45.070 --> 00:41:46.740
Now get out of here.

00:41:48.360 --> 00:41:51.190
A hundred bucks? The ad said 3000.

00:41:51.400 --> 00:41:53.780
Well, check it again, webhead.

00:41:53.950 --> 00:41:57.820
It said three grand for three minutes.
You pinned him in two.

00:41:58.020 --> 00:42:01.400
For that, I give you 100.
You're lucky to get that.

00:42:01.570 --> 00:42:02.950
I need that money.

00:42:03.410 --> 00:42:06.480
I missed the part
where that's my problem.

00:42:14.570 --> 00:42:17.900
- Hey, what the hell...?
- Put the money in the bag.

00:42:19.730 --> 00:42:21.070
Hurry up!

00:42:27.400 --> 00:42:29.480
Hey! He stole the gate!

00:42:29.650 --> 00:42:31.610
Stop that guy!

00:42:31.900 --> 00:42:34.440
Stop him! He's got my money!

00:42:34.650 --> 00:42:35.900
Thanks.

00:42:37.150 --> 00:42:39.530
What's wrong with you?
You let him go!

00:42:39.690 --> 00:42:41.950
Cut him off and call the cops!

00:42:42.110 --> 00:42:46.150
You could've taken that guy apart.
Now he'll get away.

00:42:46.310 --> 00:42:49.690
I missed the part
where that's my problem.

00:43:08.070 --> 00:43:09.280
- You gotta get back.
- I can't see. What happened?

00:43:09.280 --> 00:43:10.980
- You gotta get back.
- I can't see. What happened?

00:43:12.230 --> 00:43:13.600
Old dude, man.

00:43:13.810 --> 00:43:17.980
Come on, folks. Keep moving, please.
Keep moving. Let's go!

00:43:18.150 --> 00:43:20.980
- What happened?
- Someone got hurt.

00:43:23.350 --> 00:43:26.570
- Excuse me. Excuse me. Excuse me.
- Stay back.

00:43:27.070 --> 00:43:28.900
- Stay back!
- That's my uncle!

00:43:31.060 --> 00:43:33.690
- What happened?
- Carjacker. He's been shot.

00:43:33.810 --> 00:43:37.360
We just called the paramedics.
They're on their way.

00:43:37.570 --> 00:43:38.930
Uncle Ben?

00:43:39.850 --> 00:43:41.350
Uncle Ben.

00:43:45.110 --> 00:43:46.440
Uncle Ben?

00:43:50.060 --> 00:43:51.560
Peter.

00:43:52.440 --> 00:43:54.230
I'm here, Uncle Ben.

00:43:59.850 --> 00:44:01.060
Peter.

00:44:23.020 --> 00:44:26.050
They got the shooter.
He's headed south on Fifth.

00:44:26.260 --> 00:44:30.980
We got three cars in pursuit.
All right, folks. Come on, move back.

00:47:07.920 --> 00:47:09.840
Get a unit to the rear!

00:47:12.880 --> 00:47:14.420
I got the back!

00:47:27.340 --> 00:47:28.670
Who's there?

00:47:54.920 --> 00:47:58.050
Don't hurt me. Give me a chance.
Give me a chance!

00:47:58.210 --> 00:48:02.710
What about my uncle?
Did you give him a chance? Did you?

00:48:02.880 --> 00:48:04.380
Answer me!

00:48:07.700 --> 00:48:09.040
Stop that guy!

00:48:14.500 --> 00:48:16.210
Thanks.

00:48:26.090 --> 00:48:27.200
See you.

00:48:48.870 --> 00:48:52.330
Freeze! We've got the place
completely surrounded.

00:49:34.780 --> 00:49:37.450
Oh, no. My God.

00:49:39.330 --> 00:49:43.030
Oh, no.
Oh, my God. No!

00:49:51.360 --> 00:49:54.330
- Good evening.
- General. Good to see you.

00:49:55.120 --> 00:49:58.000
Our exoskeleton's got
real firepower, general.

00:49:58.160 --> 00:50:03.570
Well, if it does what you say it can,
I'll sign that contract tomorrow.

00:50:04.280 --> 00:50:07.830
- He's clear! Go!
- You're confident about this test?

00:50:08.000 --> 00:50:10.280
Absolutely. Curtis is our top pilot.

00:50:11.030 --> 00:50:13.780
Now, what about
your commitment to OSCORP?

00:50:13.950 --> 00:50:17.860
Nothing would please me more
than to put Osborn out of business.

00:50:20.200 --> 00:50:23.240
Preflight complete. Mark.

00:50:27.360 --> 00:50:29.990
An unidentified object
is closing fast.

00:50:30.150 --> 00:50:31.240
What's that?

00:50:31.410 --> 00:50:32.910
Can you see anything?

00:50:33.370 --> 00:50:34.740
Oh, my God!

00:50:45.030 --> 00:50:47.860
- Say "chess."
- Chess!

00:50:48.360 --> 00:50:50.240
Peter!

00:50:50.450 --> 00:50:54.980
Darling, I'm so proud of you.
You looked so handsome up there.

00:50:55.150 --> 00:50:58.650
Dad got the place in New York,
so we're all set for fall.

00:50:58.820 --> 00:51:00.360
- Great!
- You made it.

00:51:03.120 --> 00:51:06.440
It's not the first time
I've been proven wrong.

00:51:07.860 --> 00:51:10.030
- Congratulations.
- Thanks, Dad.

00:51:10.450 --> 00:51:13.030
Peter, the science award.
That's terrific.

00:51:13.440 --> 00:51:14.730
Yeah.

00:51:17.690 --> 00:51:21.070
I know this has been
a difficult time for you...

00:51:21.240 --> 00:51:24.480
...but I want you to try
to enjoy this day.

00:51:24.690 --> 00:51:26.230
Commencement:

00:51:26.400 --> 00:51:30.530
The end of one thing,
the start of something new.

00:51:32.350 --> 00:51:36.030
I don't want to be with you anymore.
Here's your ring.

00:51:36.900 --> 00:51:38.780
You know what? Whatever.

00:51:39.320 --> 00:51:40.780
Your loss.

00:51:41.480 --> 00:51:45.020
You're like a brother to Harry.
That makes you family.

00:51:45.190 --> 00:51:49.030
And if you ever need anything,
give me a call.

00:52:02.900 --> 00:52:05.150
Can I fix you something?

00:52:05.320 --> 00:52:06.820
No, thanks.

00:52:51.520 --> 00:52:53.730
I missed him a lot today.

00:52:56.310 --> 00:52:57.810
I know.

00:52:59.560 --> 00:53:01.400
I miss him too.

00:53:03.150 --> 00:53:05.470
But he was there.

00:53:08.640 --> 00:53:13.860
I can't help thinking about
the last thing I said to him.

00:53:14.140 --> 00:53:19.060
He tried to tell me something important,
and I threw it in his face.

00:53:20.810 --> 00:53:22.900
You loved him...

00:53:24.560 --> 00:53:26.810
...and he loved you.

00:53:27.680 --> 00:53:31.350
He never doubted
the man you'd grow into.

00:53:31.520 --> 00:53:34.970
How you were meant for great things.

00:53:35.510 --> 00:53:37.850
You won't disappoint him.

00:54:11.340 --> 00:54:15.510
With great power
comes great responsibility.

00:54:15.680 --> 00:54:18.880
Remember that, Pete. Remember that.

00:54:28.880 --> 00:54:30.130
Hurry up!

00:54:42.510 --> 00:54:46.270
He's not a man. My brother saw him
build a nest in Lincoln Center.

00:54:46.430 --> 00:54:49.630
I think he's human, a man.
Could be a woman.

00:54:53.720 --> 00:54:56.460
Bobby. Get a load of this!

00:54:59.630 --> 00:55:03.890
He throws up his hands,
ropes come out, and he climbs up them.

00:55:04.180 --> 00:55:08.300
I see the web, his signature,
and I know Spider-Man was here.

00:55:08.470 --> 00:55:11.090
The guy protects us,
protects the people.

00:55:11.260 --> 00:55:14.010
Some kind of freakyloo or something.

00:55:14.180 --> 00:55:16.210
He stinks and I don't like him.

00:55:16.920 --> 00:55:18.510
Don't move, lady!

00:55:26.590 --> 00:55:29.340
Guy with eight hands. Sounds hot.

00:55:29.550 --> 00:55:31.680
Those tights and that tight little...

00:55:31.840 --> 00:55:35.170
Dresses like a spider
He looks like a bug

00:55:35.380 --> 00:55:39.130
But we should all just give him
One big hug

00:55:39.340 --> 00:55:43.920
Look out
Here comes the Spider-Man

00:55:47.590 --> 00:55:51.340
"Who is Spider-Man?"
He's a criminal, that's who he is.

00:55:51.510 --> 00:55:53.630
A vigilante, a public menace.
Why's he on my front page?

00:55:53.630 --> 00:55:54.500
A vigilante, a public menace.
Why's he on my front page?

00:55:54.500 --> 00:55:55.500
A vigilante, a public menace.
Why's he on my front page?

00:55:55.500 --> 00:55:56.010
Mr. Jameson, your wife needs...

00:55:56.010 --> 00:55:57.010
Mr. Jameson, your wife needs...

00:55:58.010 --> 00:55:58.840
- There's a page six problem.
- We have a page one problem.

00:55:58.840 --> 00:56:01.170
- There's a page six problem.
- We have a page one problem.

00:56:01.330 --> 00:56:02.880
- Well?
- He's news.

00:56:03.090 --> 00:56:05.590
- The clients can't wait.
- They're about to.

00:56:05.760 --> 00:56:09.760
- He pulled six people off a subway.
- From a wreck he probably caused.

00:56:09.930 --> 00:56:14.090
Something goes wrong and he's there.
Look! He's fleeing the scene.

00:56:14.250 --> 00:56:18.220
He's probably going to save
somebody else. He's a hero!

00:56:18.380 --> 00:56:21.170
Then why the mask?
What's he got to hide?

00:56:21.330 --> 00:56:24.380
She needs to know
if you want chintz or chenille.

00:56:24.550 --> 00:56:27.010
- Whichever's cheaper.
- It's like this:

00:56:27.170 --> 00:56:31.000
We double- booked page six.
Macy's and Conway's both have...

00:56:31.170 --> 00:56:34.340
- We sold out four printings.
- Sold out?

00:56:34.500 --> 00:56:35.710
Every copy.

00:56:36.510 --> 00:56:40.080
Tomorrow, Spider-Man, page one.
Move Conway to page seven.

00:56:40.250 --> 00:56:43.170
- That's a problem.
- Then make it page eight.

00:56:43.340 --> 00:56:45.000
- That can't be done.
- Get out!

00:56:45.170 --> 00:56:50.040
We can't get a decent picture. Eddie's
on it, but we can barely see him.

00:56:50.210 --> 00:56:52.340
Aw, what is he, shy?

00:56:52.500 --> 00:56:56.510
If we can get Julia Roberts
in a thong, we can get this weirdo.

00:56:56.660 --> 00:57:00.080
On the front page:
"Cash for a Spider-Man picture."

00:57:00.250 --> 00:57:03.710
He doesn't want to be famous?
I'll make him infamous!

00:57:16.160 --> 00:57:17.580
Buzz off.

00:57:18.290 --> 00:57:21.250
- M.J., it's me, Peter.
- Hi!

00:57:22.960 --> 00:57:27.830
- What are you doing around here?
- Begging for a job. How about you?

00:57:28.330 --> 00:57:32.040
- I'm headed to an audition.
- An audition? So you're acting?

00:57:32.210 --> 00:57:33.250
Yeah.

00:57:33.460 --> 00:57:37.330
I work steady.
In fact, I just got off a job.

00:57:37.500 --> 00:57:38.660
That's great.

00:57:39.250 --> 00:57:42.460
- You're doing it. Living your dream.
- Glamour girl!

00:57:42.630 --> 00:57:44.240
Your drawer was short $6!

00:57:44.410 --> 00:57:47.040
Next time, I'll take it
from your check.

00:57:48.120 --> 00:57:51.920
Excuse me, Miss Watson?
I'm talking to you! Hey!

00:57:52.130 --> 00:57:54.410
Yes, Enrique! Okay? I get you.

00:57:54.580 --> 00:57:58.710
It better not happen no more.
Don't roll your eyes at me.

00:58:05.660 --> 00:58:07.370
Some dream, huh?

00:58:08.250 --> 00:58:10.880
It's nothing to be
embarrassed about.

00:58:11.030 --> 00:58:13.830
- Don't tell Harry.
- Don't tell Harry?

00:58:14.240 --> 00:58:18.830
Don't you guys live together?
We're going out. Didn't he tell you?

00:58:19.250 --> 00:58:20.820
Oh, yeah. Right.

00:58:21.070 --> 00:58:24.160
I think he'd hate the idea
of my waiting tables.

00:58:24.330 --> 00:58:28.750
- He'd think it was low or something.
- It's not low. You have a job.

00:58:29.080 --> 00:58:33.410
You know, Harry doesn't live on
a little place I like to call Earth.

00:58:34.910 --> 00:58:36.830
No, I guess not.

00:58:41.820 --> 00:58:43.410
Thanks, Pete.

00:58:44.830 --> 00:58:46.750
We should catch up sometime.

00:58:50.950 --> 00:58:53.490
Let's get some lunch some evening.

00:58:54.740 --> 00:58:59.240
I'll come by and have some of your
Moondance coffee some day.

00:58:59.450 --> 00:59:02.160
- And I won't tell Harry.
- Don't tell Harry.

00:59:02.330 --> 00:59:03.580
I won't.

00:59:05.750 --> 00:59:07.490
I won't tell Harry.

00:59:18.780 --> 00:59:21.240
Timing's perfect. Hey.

00:59:21.450 --> 00:59:24.740
Five new contracts. It'll be great.

00:59:26.860 --> 00:59:29.570
Norman's making his weekly inspection.

00:59:30.370 --> 00:59:32.620
Spent half of it on the phone.

00:59:33.200 --> 00:59:37.900
Look, man, I'm glad you're here.
I need your help. I'm really lost here.

00:59:38.740 --> 00:59:40.030
Are you all right?

00:59:41.370 --> 00:59:45.900
You look like you just got
second place in the science fair.

00:59:47.200 --> 00:59:50.160
I was late for work
and Dr. Connors fired me.

00:59:50.320 --> 00:59:51.870
You were late again?

00:59:52.490 --> 00:59:56.440
I don't get it.
Where do you go all the time?

00:59:56.610 --> 00:59:57.860
Around.

00:59:58.030 --> 00:59:59.740
Peter Parker.

01:00:00.070 --> 01:00:02.570
- Maybe you'll tell me who she is.
- Who?

01:00:02.730 --> 01:00:05.820
- This mystery girl Harry's been dating.
- Dad.

01:00:06.190 --> 01:00:07.860
When do I get to meet her?

01:00:08.030 --> 01:00:11.320
Well, sorry.
Harry hasn't mentioned her.

01:00:14.190 --> 01:00:17.450
Pete, you're probably looking
for a job now, right?

01:00:17.650 --> 01:00:20.490
Dad, maybe you can help him out.

01:00:20.660 --> 01:00:24.980
- I appreciate it, but I'll be fine.
- I'll make a few calls.

01:00:25.150 --> 01:00:29.450
I couldn't accept it. I like to earn
what I get. I'll find work.

01:00:29.660 --> 01:00:31.270
I respect that.

01:00:31.980 --> 01:00:34.110
You want to make it on your own.

01:00:34.780 --> 01:00:36.110
That's great.

01:00:36.990 --> 01:00:39.320
What other skills do you have?

01:00:39.520 --> 01:00:41.650
I was thinking about photography.

01:00:44.610 --> 01:00:45.860
Hello.

01:00:47.780 --> 01:00:50.060
Let's go! Move it!

01:00:51.230 --> 01:00:52.900
Watch the street!

01:01:08.310 --> 01:01:09.690
Cheese!

01:01:18.600 --> 01:01:19.900
They're crap.

01:01:20.100 --> 01:01:23.070
Crap, crap. Megacrap.

01:01:23.270 --> 01:01:26.430
- I'll give you $200.
- That seems a little low.

01:01:26.640 --> 01:01:28.390
Take them somewhere else.

01:01:28.810 --> 01:01:32.900
- Your wife says the tile's out of stock.
- We'll put a rug there.

01:01:33.270 --> 01:01:35.230
Sit down. Give me that.

01:01:36.810 --> 01:01:39.350
Give you 300.
That's the standard fee.

01:01:39.520 --> 01:01:41.860
- Scrap page one. Run that.
- Headline?

01:01:42.150 --> 01:01:45.350
"Spider-Man, Hero or Menace?
Exclusive Photos."

01:01:45.520 --> 01:01:48.650
- Menace? He was protecting...
- You take the photos...

01:01:48.850 --> 01:01:51.520
...l'll make up the headlines. Okay?

01:01:51.690 --> 01:01:53.680
- Yes, sir.
- Goody.

01:01:54.140 --> 01:01:57.640
Give this to the girl up front.
She'll see you get paid.

01:01:58.100 --> 01:02:00.900
- I'd like a job, sir.
- No jobs. Freelance.

01:02:01.110 --> 01:02:02.730
Best thing for you.

01:02:02.940 --> 01:02:07.230
You bring me more shots of that clown,
maybe I'll buy them.

01:02:07.440 --> 01:02:10.400
But I never said you have a job. Meat.

01:02:10.560 --> 01:02:14.850
I'll send you a box of Christmas
meat. Bring me more photos.

01:02:16.430 --> 01:02:17.640
- Hi.
- Hi.

01:02:17.850 --> 01:02:21.270
Mr. Jameson told me
to give that to you.

01:02:22.350 --> 01:02:25.480
- Welcome to the Daily Bugle.
- Thank you.

01:02:26.020 --> 01:02:27.390
I'm Peter Parker.

01:02:29.900 --> 01:02:32.060
I'm a photographer.

01:02:32.850 --> 01:02:35.390
Yes. I can see that.

01:02:43.100 --> 01:02:44.930
As of today...

01:02:45.100 --> 01:02:49.100
...OSCORP Industries has surpassed
Quest Aerospace...

01:02:49.350 --> 01:02:53.770
...as the principal supplier
to the United States military.

01:02:53.930 --> 01:02:56.770
In short, ladies and gentlemen
of the board...

01:02:56.940 --> 01:03:00.090
...costs are down, revenues are up...

01:03:00.350 --> 01:03:03.180
...and our stock
has never been higher.

01:03:03.350 --> 01:03:07.770
Wonderful news, Norman.
That's why we're selling the company.

01:03:08.590 --> 01:03:09.840
What?

01:03:10.050 --> 01:03:15.180
Quest is recapitalizing in the wake
of the bombing. Expanding.

01:03:15.430 --> 01:03:18.180
They made a tender offer
we can't ignore.

01:03:18.340 --> 01:03:19.510
Why wasn't I told?

01:03:19.680 --> 01:03:23.770
They don't want a power struggle
with entrenched management.

01:03:24.060 --> 01:03:26.350
The deal is off if you come with it.

01:03:26.510 --> 01:03:29.930
The board expects your resignation
in 30 days.

01:03:30.140 --> 01:03:32.100
You can't do this to me.

01:03:35.270 --> 01:03:37.550
I started this company.

01:03:38.590 --> 01:03:41.010
You know how much I sacrificed?!

01:03:44.850 --> 01:03:50.300
- Oh, Max. Please.
- Norman, the board is unanimous.

01:03:50.850 --> 01:03:54.840
We're announcing the sale
after the World Unity Festival.

01:03:55.010 --> 01:03:56.510
I'm sorry.

01:03:57.510 --> 01:03:59.640
You're out, Norman.

01:04:09.510 --> 01:04:11.010
Am I?

01:04:14.800 --> 01:04:15.470
Welcome to OSCORP Industries
Unity Day Festival.

01:04:15.470 --> 01:04:17.970
Welcome to OSCORP Industries
Unity Day Festival.

01:04:17.970 --> 01:04:18.970
Let's hear it for Macy Gray.

01:04:18.970 --> 01:04:19.470
Let's hear it for Macy Gray.

01:04:19.470 --> 01:04:20.010
Let's hear it for Macy Gray.

01:04:20.010 --> 01:04:21.720
Let's hear it for Macy Gray.

01:04:58.090 --> 01:05:01.630
M.J., why didn't you wear
the black dress?

01:05:02.670 --> 01:05:06.340
Just, I wanted to impress my father.
He loves black.

01:05:06.510 --> 01:05:11.040
Well, maybe he'll be impressed
no matter what. You think I'm pretty.

01:05:11.590 --> 01:05:13.960
I think you're beautiful.

01:05:26.760 --> 01:05:30.000
I forgot my drink inside.

01:05:40.210 --> 01:05:42.340
- Oh, hi, Mr. Fargas.
- Oh, Harry.

01:05:43.420 --> 01:05:48.580
- Have you seen my father?
- Well, I'm not sure if he's coming.

01:06:00.590 --> 01:06:03.090
- What is that?
- Must be new this year.

01:06:07.960 --> 01:06:09.250
What is that?

01:06:09.420 --> 01:06:11.340
That's our glider!

01:06:21.710 --> 01:06:23.160
What the hell was that?

01:06:51.540 --> 01:06:52.950
Code three!

01:07:08.960 --> 01:07:11.120
- Oh, my God! Harry!
- M.J.!

01:07:17.080 --> 01:07:20.530
Harry! Help me! Harry!

01:07:26.500 --> 01:07:28.240
Out, am I?

01:07:32.790 --> 01:07:36.000
- Mary Jane!
- Harry!

01:07:37.990 --> 01:07:39.870
Hello, my dear.

01:07:40.870 --> 01:07:42.700
It's Spider-Man!

01:07:54.200 --> 01:07:56.150
- Come on. Move, kid.
- Billy!

01:07:59.660 --> 01:08:01.990
Somebody help him!

01:08:02.200 --> 01:08:04.250
No!

01:08:05.240 --> 01:08:06.780
Mommy!

01:08:08.780 --> 01:08:10.740
- Hold it!
- I surrender.

01:08:11.330 --> 01:08:13.830
- Oh, boy.
- Hold it right there!

01:08:19.620 --> 01:08:20.870
Lmpressive.

01:08:45.110 --> 01:08:48.570
- Mary Jane!
- Help! Someone please help me!

01:09:13.900 --> 01:09:14.950
Hold on!

01:09:16.570 --> 01:09:17.610
Watch out!

01:09:26.740 --> 01:09:30.520
We'll meet again, Spider-Man!

01:10:15.980 --> 01:10:18.650
Well, beats taking the subway.

01:10:18.860 --> 01:10:22.110
Don't mind us.
She just needs to use the elevator.

01:10:22.280 --> 01:10:23.400
Wait.

01:10:23.570 --> 01:10:24.810
Who are you?

01:10:24.980 --> 01:10:27.560
- You know who I am.
- I do?

01:10:27.770 --> 01:10:30.400
Your friendly neighborhood Spider-Man.

01:10:42.110 --> 01:10:45.980
Incredible?
What do you mean he's incredible?

01:10:47.150 --> 01:10:50.820
No. All right, wait.
Stay there. I'll come over.

01:10:51.480 --> 01:10:53.140
No, I'm gonna come...

01:10:53.480 --> 01:10:56.900
All right. Fine.
Will you call me in the morning?

01:10:57.100 --> 01:11:00.070
And we'll go and have breakfast and...

01:11:00.230 --> 01:11:02.520
...I want to buy you something.

01:11:02.680 --> 01:11:06.020
Because I want to.
It'll make you feel better.

01:11:07.060 --> 01:11:10.720
Okay. And what do you mean,
incredible?

01:11:13.560 --> 01:11:15.940
All right. I'm sorry. Sleep tight.

01:11:16.100 --> 01:11:17.850
Don't let the bedbugs...

01:11:23.520 --> 01:11:26.560
She's all right.
She's just a little rattled.

01:11:28.270 --> 01:11:31.890
Look, Pete, I should have
told you about us.

01:11:33.230 --> 01:11:35.890
But you should know
I'm crazy about her.

01:11:36.060 --> 01:11:39.100
It's just, you know,
you never made a move.

01:11:40.180 --> 01:11:41.680
You're right.

01:11:42.600 --> 01:11:44.100
I didn't.

01:11:48.100 --> 01:11:50.510
I'm gonna get some rest.

01:11:51.770 --> 01:11:54.020
I'm gonna stay up for a while.

01:11:55.100 --> 01:11:56.850
What was that thing?

01:11:57.430 --> 01:11:58.760
I don't know.

01:12:00.180 --> 01:12:03.560
Whatever it is,
somebody has to stop it.

01:12:19.430 --> 01:12:20.930
Somebody there?

01:12:20.930 --> 01:12:21.720
Somebody.

01:12:21.720 --> 01:12:23.390
Somebody.

01:12:24.730 --> 01:12:26.260
Who said that?

01:12:26.930 --> 01:12:30.260
Don't play the innocent with me.

01:12:32.720 --> 01:12:35.380
You've known all along.

01:12:39.390 --> 01:12:40.760
Where are you?

01:12:40.930 --> 01:12:44.970
Follow the cold shiver
running down your spine.

01:12:51.850 --> 01:12:53.670
I'm right here.

01:12:55.430 --> 01:12:57.430
I don't understand.

01:12:58.430 --> 01:13:01.600
Did you think it was coincidence?

01:13:01.850 --> 01:13:05.380
So many good things,
all happening for you.

01:13:05.550 --> 01:13:09.220
All for you. Norman.

01:13:11.760 --> 01:13:13.170
What do you want?

01:13:13.720 --> 01:13:15.760
To say what you won't.

01:13:16.050 --> 01:13:18.600
To do what you can't.

01:13:18.760 --> 01:13:23.340
To remove those in your way.

01:13:27.300 --> 01:13:29.260
The board members.

01:13:30.550 --> 01:13:31.920
You killed them.

01:13:32.090 --> 01:13:33.630
We killed them.

01:13:33.970 --> 01:13:35.010
We?

01:13:35.220 --> 01:13:36.760
Remember?

01:13:36.930 --> 01:13:39.590
Your little accident
in the laboratory.

01:13:41.460 --> 01:13:43.260
The performance enhancers.

01:13:43.420 --> 01:13:48.710
Bingo. Me!
Your greatest creation.

01:13:48.920 --> 01:13:52.710
Bringing you
what you've always wanted:

01:13:52.880 --> 01:13:55.760
Power beyond your wildest dreams.

01:13:55.930 --> 01:13:58.420
And it's only the beginning.

01:13:59.920 --> 01:14:04.260
There's only one who can stop us.

01:14:05.050 --> 01:14:08.420
Or imagine if he joined us.

01:14:13.220 --> 01:14:16.420
Spider-Man. And the Green Goblin.

01:14:16.670 --> 01:14:19.920
The Green Goblin. You like that?
Made it up myself.

01:14:20.090 --> 01:14:23.090
- These weirdos all got to have a name.
- Mr. Jameson...

01:14:23.260 --> 01:14:24.930
- Hoffman!
- Yeah?

01:14:26.130 --> 01:14:29.880
Copyright "Green Goblin."
I want a quarter every time it's said.

01:14:30.090 --> 01:14:32.380
How about "Green Meanie"?

01:14:32.550 --> 01:14:35.420
Spider-Man wasn't attacking.
That's slander.

01:14:35.580 --> 01:14:37.920
It is not. I resent that.

01:14:38.170 --> 01:14:40.920
Slander is spoken.
In print, it's libel.

01:14:41.090 --> 01:14:42.760
You don't trust anybody.

01:14:43.220 --> 01:14:44.960
I trust my barber.

01:14:45.790 --> 01:14:47.290
Are you his lawyer?

01:14:47.500 --> 01:14:52.260
Let him sue. Get rich like a normal
person. That's what made this country...

01:14:59.750 --> 01:15:02.870
Jameson, you slime.

01:15:03.080 --> 01:15:06.380
Who takes the pictures of Spider-Man?

01:15:06.580 --> 01:15:09.500
- I don't know. His stuff comes by mail.
- Liar!

01:15:09.670 --> 01:15:12.660
- I swear.
- He's the one who can bring me to him.

01:15:12.830 --> 01:15:15.750
- I don't know who he is.
- You are useless.

01:15:15.960 --> 01:15:18.210
Set him down, tough guy.

01:15:18.460 --> 01:15:23.040
- Speak of the devil.
- I knew you two were in this together!

01:15:23.250 --> 01:15:25.830
Kiddo, let Mom and Dad
talk for a minute.

01:15:26.040 --> 01:15:28.500
Sleep...

01:15:42.960 --> 01:15:46.960
Wake up, little spider. Wake up.

01:15:47.130 --> 01:15:51.540
No, you're not dead yet.

01:15:51.750 --> 01:15:53.910
Just paralyzed...

01:15:54.080 --> 01:15:56.040
...temporarily.

01:15:57.040 --> 01:16:00.120
You're an amazing creature,
Spider-Man.

01:16:00.330 --> 01:16:03.000
You and I are not so different.

01:16:03.710 --> 01:16:07.040
I'm not like you. You're a murderer.

01:16:07.250 --> 01:16:10.120
Well, to each his own.

01:16:10.290 --> 01:16:13.250
I chose my path,
you chose the way of the hero.

01:16:13.910 --> 01:16:18.530
And they found you amusing
for a while, the people of this city.

01:16:18.740 --> 01:16:22.000
But the one thing they love
more than a hero...

01:16:22.200 --> 01:16:25.790
...is to see a hero fail,
fall, die trying.

01:16:25.960 --> 01:16:30.490
In spite of everything you've done for
them, eventually, they will hate you.

01:16:30.700 --> 01:16:31.750
Why bother?

01:16:31.950 --> 01:16:36.660
- Because it's right.
- Here's the real truth.

01:16:37.070 --> 01:16:40.080
There are eight million people
in this city.

01:16:40.290 --> 01:16:44.580
And those teeming masses exist
for the sole purpose...

01:16:44.780 --> 01:16:48.740
...of lifting the few exceptional
people onto their shoulders.

01:16:48.910 --> 01:16:50.330
You, me...

01:16:50.910 --> 01:16:52.830
...we're exceptional.

01:16:53.080 --> 01:16:57.740
I could squash you like a bug
right now.

01:16:57.950 --> 01:17:01.620
But I'm offering you a choice.
Join me.

01:17:01.790 --> 01:17:05.360
Imagine what we could
accomplish together.

01:17:05.570 --> 01:17:08.330
What we could create.

01:17:08.910 --> 01:17:10.910
Or we could destroy.

01:17:11.080 --> 01:17:15.030
Cause the deaths of countless
innocents in selfish battle...

01:17:15.240 --> 01:17:20.120
...again and again and again until
we're both dead. Is that what you want?

01:17:22.110 --> 01:17:24.990
Think about it, hero.

01:17:36.950 --> 01:17:42.280
In spite of everything you've done for
them, eventually, they will hate you.

01:17:52.610 --> 01:17:54.070
It's me again.

01:17:54.450 --> 01:17:55.870
How was your audition?

01:17:56.070 --> 01:17:59.070
- How'd you know?
- The hot line. Your mom...

01:17:59.230 --> 01:18:01.190
...told my aunt, told me.

01:18:01.650 --> 01:18:02.990
So you just came by?

01:18:03.200 --> 01:18:06.820
I was in the neighborhood.
Needed to see a friendly face.

01:18:06.990 --> 01:18:11.570
I took two buses and a cab
to get in the neighborhood, but...

01:18:11.820 --> 01:18:13.320
So how'd it go?

01:18:15.490 --> 01:18:18.070
They said I needed acting lessons.

01:18:18.230 --> 01:18:21.990
A soap opera told me
I needed acting lessons.

01:18:22.150 --> 01:18:27.480
Let me buy you a cheeseburger.
The sky's the limit, up to $7.84.

01:18:28.820 --> 01:18:30.900
I'd like a cheeseburger.

01:18:31.360 --> 01:18:34.820
Oh, but I'm going out to dinner
with Harry.

01:18:35.240 --> 01:18:36.650
Come with us.

01:18:36.810 --> 01:18:39.570
No, thanks. How's it going with...?

01:18:41.490 --> 01:18:43.990
Never mind.
That's none of my business.

01:18:44.490 --> 01:18:45.980
It's not?

01:18:47.400 --> 01:18:49.070
Why so interested?

01:18:49.730 --> 01:18:51.240
I'm not.

01:18:51.490 --> 01:18:52.860
You're not?

01:18:54.490 --> 01:18:57.230
- Well, why would I be?
- I don't know.

01:18:57.480 --> 01:18:59.280
Why would you be?

01:19:01.150 --> 01:19:03.490
I, that's a...

01:19:03.700 --> 01:19:05.190
I don't know.

01:19:07.400 --> 01:19:10.230
Sorry you won't come with us.

01:19:12.700 --> 01:19:14.650
I'd better run, tiger.

01:19:23.350 --> 01:19:25.350
Hey, check it out, man.

01:19:25.520 --> 01:19:27.190
Come on, man.

01:19:30.740 --> 01:19:33.980
Hey, where you going, baby?
Come on!

01:19:51.850 --> 01:19:53.310
Get off me!

01:20:26.560 --> 01:20:28.060
Wait!

01:20:32.890 --> 01:20:35.270
You have a knack
for getting in trouble.

01:20:35.440 --> 01:20:39.810
You have a knack for saving my life.
I think I have a superhero stalker.

01:20:40.020 --> 01:20:41.890
I was in the neighborhood.

01:20:43.770 --> 01:20:46.390
You are amazing.

01:20:47.350 --> 01:20:50.060
Some people don't think so.

01:20:51.140 --> 01:20:54.150
- But you are.
- Nice to have a fan.

01:20:54.900 --> 01:20:58.100
Do I get to say thank you this time?

01:20:58.970 --> 01:21:00.470
Wait.

01:22:09.390 --> 01:22:11.510
Let me in! My baby's in there!

01:22:11.670 --> 01:22:13.800
- Let me go!
- The roof's collapsing!

01:22:13.970 --> 01:22:17.470
- Somebody save my baby!
- The roof's about to collapse!

01:22:17.680 --> 01:22:19.010
Look! Up there!

01:22:25.600 --> 01:22:27.430
Save my baby, please!

01:22:51.130 --> 01:22:52.260
No!

01:23:00.010 --> 01:23:04.010
- It's okay. Your baby's fine.
- Oh, my baby!

01:23:05.050 --> 01:23:07.960
God bless you, Spider-Man.
Bless you.

01:23:08.170 --> 01:23:09.920
Don't let him get away!

01:23:10.130 --> 01:23:13.380
Hold it! You're under arrest.
I'm taking you in.

01:23:13.550 --> 01:23:16.880
Oh, my God, there's somebody
still up there!

01:23:18.340 --> 01:23:19.670
I'm going.

01:23:21.340 --> 01:23:24.380
- I'll be here when you get back.
- Not coming back.

01:23:24.790 --> 01:23:25.920
Go! Go!

01:23:34.830 --> 01:23:36.540
Where are you?

01:23:38.590 --> 01:23:40.170
Where are you?

01:23:45.540 --> 01:23:47.920
I'm gonna get you out of here!

01:23:50.510 --> 01:23:52.000
It's okay.

01:23:59.050 --> 01:24:01.620
You're pathetically predictable.

01:24:01.790 --> 01:24:03.710
Like a moth to the flame.

01:24:04.580 --> 01:24:07.040
What about my generous proposal?

01:24:08.090 --> 01:24:10.910
Are you in or are you out?

01:24:11.120 --> 01:24:17.040
- It's you who's out. Out of your mind.
- Wrong answer.

01:24:17.460 --> 01:24:18.960
Oh, great.

01:24:57.580 --> 01:25:00.370
No one says no to me!

01:25:07.700 --> 01:25:11.120
- M.J., will you stop goofing around?
- Harry, relax.

01:25:13.620 --> 01:25:14.880
He's here.

01:25:15.660 --> 01:25:17.160
Are you ready?

01:25:19.000 --> 01:25:21.660
Aunt May. I'm sorry I'm late.

01:25:21.870 --> 01:25:24.950
Work was murder.
I picked up a fruitcake.

01:25:25.160 --> 01:25:28.580
Thank you, Mr. Osborn.
We're so glad you could come.

01:25:28.830 --> 01:25:31.540
Who is this lovely young lady?

01:25:31.710 --> 01:25:35.990
I'd like you to meet my father.
Dad, this is Mary Jane Watson.

01:25:36.200 --> 01:25:38.870
I've been looking forward
to meeting you.

01:25:39.080 --> 01:25:42.790
- Happy Thanksgiving, sir.
- Now, where is Peter?

01:25:42.960 --> 01:25:45.330
He'd better remember
that cranberry sauce.

01:25:51.080 --> 01:25:54.660
Oh, that's weird.
I didn't know he was here.

01:25:57.660 --> 01:25:59.160
Peter?

01:26:07.200 --> 01:26:08.910
Is that you?

01:26:14.370 --> 01:26:18.540
How strange. There's nobody here.

01:26:24.990 --> 01:26:29.450
- Bit of a slob, isn't he?
- All brilliant men are.

01:27:02.030 --> 01:27:04.660
- Hey, everyone.
- Oh, Peter!

01:27:04.820 --> 01:27:06.580
It's a jungle out there.

01:27:06.730 --> 01:27:10.650
Had to beat an old lady with a stick
to get these cranberries.

01:27:11.110 --> 01:27:13.950
Thank you.
Now then, everybody sit down...

01:27:14.120 --> 01:27:15.700
...and we can say grace.

01:27:19.240 --> 01:27:20.990
Here we go.

01:27:27.940 --> 01:27:30.280
- There we are.
- It looks delicious.

01:27:34.070 --> 01:27:36.360
Will you do the honors?

01:27:48.030 --> 01:27:51.280
Why, Peter, you're bleeding.

01:27:54.110 --> 01:27:59.440
I stepped off a curb and got clipped
by one of those bike messengers.

01:27:59.610 --> 01:28:01.150
Well, let me see.

01:28:01.360 --> 01:28:02.850
Oh, my goodness.

01:28:03.100 --> 01:28:05.520
- That looks awful.
- No, it's nothing.

01:28:05.690 --> 01:28:08.820
I'll get the first-aid kit.
Then we'll say grace.

01:28:09.030 --> 01:28:14.310
This is the boys' first Thanksgiving
here, and we'll do things properly.

01:28:15.270 --> 01:28:18.360
How did you say that happened?

01:28:18.780 --> 01:28:20.490
Bike messenger.

01:28:20.700 --> 01:28:22.650
Knocked me down.

01:28:28.030 --> 01:28:31.690
- If you'll excuse me, I've got to go.
- Why?

01:28:32.600 --> 01:28:35.980
Something has come to my attention.

01:28:36.190 --> 01:28:37.440
Are you all right?

01:28:37.650 --> 01:28:41.140
I'm fine, just fine.
Thank you, Mrs. Parker. Everyone.

01:28:41.770 --> 01:28:44.150
- Enjoy the fruitcake.
- Dad!

01:28:46.320 --> 01:28:50.100
I planned this so you'd meet M.J.,
and now you have to leave?

01:28:50.310 --> 01:28:51.980
I've got to go.

01:28:52.310 --> 01:28:56.440
- This girl is important to me.
- Harry, please. Look at her.

01:28:56.650 --> 01:29:00.600
Think she's sniffing around
because she likes your personality?

01:29:00.850 --> 01:29:03.860
- What are you saying?
- Your mother was beautiful.

01:29:04.020 --> 01:29:09.430
They're all beautiful until they're
snarling after your money like wolves.

01:29:09.640 --> 01:29:10.890
You're wrong, Dad.

01:29:11.440 --> 01:29:14.650
A word to the not-so-wise
about your girlfriend:

01:29:14.810 --> 01:29:18.680
Do what you need to with her,
then broom her fast.

01:29:29.060 --> 01:29:31.600
Thanks for sticking up for me, Harry.

01:29:31.810 --> 01:29:34.770
- You heard?
- Everyone heard that creep.

01:29:34.980 --> 01:29:38.850
That creep is my father.
With luck, I'll be half of what he is.

01:29:39.100 --> 01:29:41.440
Shut up about stuff
you don't understand!

01:29:41.600 --> 01:29:43.270
Harry Osborn!

01:29:44.360 --> 01:29:46.390
I'm sorry, Aunt May.

01:29:49.350 --> 01:29:52.690
Spider-Man is all but invincible.

01:29:52.850 --> 01:29:55.970
But Parker, we can destroy him.

01:29:56.180 --> 01:29:57.520
I can't.

01:29:57.680 --> 01:30:00.690
Betrayal must not be countenanced.

01:30:00.940 --> 01:30:03.180
Parker must be educated.

01:30:05.350 --> 01:30:06.640
What do I do?

01:30:06.850 --> 01:30:10.940
Instruct him in the matters
of loss and pain.

01:30:11.100 --> 01:30:14.140
Make him suffer.
Make him wish he were dead.

01:30:14.390 --> 01:30:15.680
Yes?

01:30:15.850 --> 01:30:17.770
And then grant his wish.

01:30:18.680 --> 01:30:19.980
But how?

01:30:20.190 --> 01:30:24.470
The cunning warrior attacks
neither body nor mind.

01:30:24.680 --> 01:30:25.850
Tell me how!

01:30:26.010 --> 01:30:28.180
The heart, Osborn.

01:30:28.430 --> 01:30:31.470
First, we attack his heart.

01:30:33.350 --> 01:30:36.850
Give us this day our daily bread,
and forgive us our trespasses...

01:30:37.060 --> 01:30:40.020
...as we forgive those
who trespass against us.

01:30:40.260 --> 01:30:44.100
Lead us not into temptation,
but deliver us...

01:30:51.840 --> 01:30:54.390
Deliver us!

01:30:54.600 --> 01:30:55.970
Finish it!

01:30:56.260 --> 01:31:00.180
- Finish it!
- From evil!

01:31:05.890 --> 01:31:08.050
Two milligrams IV.

01:31:09.840 --> 01:31:11.090
Get the BP.

01:31:11.510 --> 01:31:15.100
Aunt May. Is she gonna be okay?
What happened?

01:31:15.310 --> 01:31:16.640
You have to leave.

01:31:16.810 --> 01:31:18.510
- What happened?
- Those eyes!

01:31:18.670 --> 01:31:22.760
Those horrible yellow eyes!

01:31:27.590 --> 01:31:30.130
He knows who I am.

01:32:14.040 --> 01:32:15.630
I'm sorry.

01:32:19.340 --> 01:32:21.800
- Will she be okay?
- She'll be fine.

01:32:21.970 --> 01:32:24.630
She's been sleeping all day.

01:32:25.630 --> 01:32:28.380
- Thanks for coming.
- Of course.

01:32:32.540 --> 01:32:35.460
How are you?
You okay about the other night?

01:32:35.630 --> 01:32:39.340
Yeah, I'm fine. I just felt bad
about leaving Aunt May.

01:32:39.550 --> 01:32:42.500
- Have you talked to Harry?
- He called me.

01:32:42.960 --> 01:32:45.130
I haven't called him back.

01:32:47.210 --> 01:32:48.920
The fact is...

01:32:50.080 --> 01:32:52.920
...l'm in love with somebody else.
- You are?

01:32:53.080 --> 01:32:55.300
At least I think I am.

01:32:56.960 --> 01:33:00.000
- It's not the time to talk about it.
- No. Go on.

01:33:00.170 --> 01:33:03.420
Would I know his name, this guy?

01:33:03.630 --> 01:33:06.510
You'll think I'm a little girl
with a crush.

01:33:06.670 --> 01:33:08.050
Trust me.

01:33:08.300 --> 01:33:09.540
It's funny.

01:33:11.540 --> 01:33:15.500
He's saved my life twice,
and I've never even seen his face.

01:33:15.670 --> 01:33:19.040
- Oh. Him.
- You're laughing at me.

01:33:19.250 --> 01:33:22.210
No, I understand.
He is extremely cool.

01:33:22.420 --> 01:33:26.710
But do you think it's true,
all the terrible things they say?

01:33:26.880 --> 01:33:29.790
Not Spider-Man,
not a chance in the world.

01:33:30.000 --> 01:33:31.630
I know him a little bit.

01:33:31.830 --> 01:33:34.710
I'm sort of his unofficial
photographer.

01:33:34.920 --> 01:33:38.040
- Has he mentioned me?
- Yeah.

01:33:38.370 --> 01:33:39.830
What'd he say?

01:33:40.420 --> 01:33:41.750
I said...

01:33:42.830 --> 01:33:47.120
He asked me what I thought about you.

01:33:48.040 --> 01:33:50.080
And what did you say?

01:33:50.790 --> 01:33:54.880
I said, "Spider-Man."

01:33:55.200 --> 01:34:00.080
I said, "The great thing about M. J...

01:34:00.290 --> 01:34:01.830
...is...

01:34:02.750 --> 01:34:05.990
...when you look in her eyes...

01:34:08.540 --> 01:34:11.750
...and she's looking back in yours...

01:34:12.750 --> 01:34:15.740
...everything feels...

01:34:16.950 --> 01:34:18.790
...not quite normal.

01:34:20.040 --> 01:34:21.830
Because you feel...

01:34:22.380 --> 01:34:23.990
...stronger...

01:34:25.540 --> 01:34:29.160
...and weaker at the same time.

01:34:30.210 --> 01:34:32.320
You feel excited...

01:34:33.200 --> 01:34:35.240
...and at the same time...

01:34:35.870 --> 01:34:37.500
...terrified.

01:34:39.830 --> 01:34:44.120
The truth is, you don't know
what you feel...

01:34:45.540 --> 01:34:49.160
...except you know what kind of man
you want to be.

01:34:51.870 --> 01:34:53.740
It's as if you've...

01:34:54.370 --> 01:34:57.540
...reached the unreachable...

01:34:59.120 --> 01:35:01.820
...and you weren't ready for it."

01:35:05.290 --> 01:35:07.040
You said that?

01:35:07.830 --> 01:35:10.160
Well, something like that.

01:35:54.410 --> 01:35:55.900
Dad?

01:36:01.240 --> 01:36:03.330
Dad, is that you?

01:36:09.910 --> 01:36:11.410
What is it?

01:36:13.660 --> 01:36:18.650
You were right about M.J.
You're right about everything.

01:36:19.660 --> 01:36:22.370
She's in love with Peter.

01:36:22.660 --> 01:36:24.440
- Parker?
- Yeah.

01:36:24.610 --> 01:36:27.740
And how does he feel about her?

01:36:29.150 --> 01:36:31.700
He's loved her since the 4th grade.

01:36:32.660 --> 01:36:37.900
He pretends like he doesn't, but
there's no one Peter cares for more.

01:36:40.820 --> 01:36:42.560
I'm so sorry.

01:36:45.030 --> 01:36:48.490
I haven't always been there for you,
have I?

01:36:50.240 --> 01:36:53.440
You're busy. You're an important man.
I understand.

01:36:53.610 --> 01:36:55.440
That's no excuse.

01:36:56.440 --> 01:36:58.240
I'm proud of you.

01:36:58.780 --> 01:37:03.650
I've lost sight of that somewhere.
But I'll make it up to you.

01:37:03.820 --> 01:37:07.070
I'm going to rectify
certain inequities.

01:37:21.190 --> 01:37:22.980
Wake up, little spider.

01:37:23.150 --> 01:37:24.650
Wake up.

01:37:25.980 --> 01:37:27.570
Go home, dear.

01:37:27.780 --> 01:37:29.100
You look awful.

01:37:29.310 --> 01:37:31.610
- And you look beautiful.
- Thank you.

01:37:31.770 --> 01:37:35.110
- I don't like to leave you here.
- But I'm safe here.

01:37:35.280 --> 01:37:37.980
- Can I do anything for you?
- You do too much.

01:37:38.140 --> 01:37:43.690
College, a job, all this time with me.
You're not Superman, you know.

01:37:44.440 --> 01:37:46.190
A smile. Finally.

01:37:46.360 --> 01:37:50.690
Haven't seen one of those on your face
since Mary Jane was here.

01:37:50.850 --> 01:37:53.150
You were supposed to be asleep.

01:37:53.980 --> 01:37:58.730
You know, you were about 6 years old
when M.J.'s family moved in next door.

01:37:58.940 --> 01:38:02.940
When she got out of the car,
and you saw her for the first time...

01:38:03.150 --> 01:38:09.390
...you grabbed me and said,
"Aunt May, is that an angel?"

01:38:09.600 --> 01:38:13.150
- Gee, did I say that?
- You sure did.

01:38:15.810 --> 01:38:18.560
Well, Harry's in love with her.

01:38:18.770 --> 01:38:22.520
- She's still his girl.
- Well, isn't that up to her?

01:38:22.730 --> 01:38:27.310
- She doesn't really know who I am.
- Because you won't let her.

01:38:27.520 --> 01:38:30.650
You're so mysterious all the time.

01:38:30.900 --> 01:38:33.640
Tell me, would it be so dangerous...

01:38:33.850 --> 01:38:37.810
...to let Mary Jane know
how much you care?

01:38:38.270 --> 01:38:40.690
Everybody else knows.

01:38:43.600 --> 01:38:44.890
I'll be right back.

01:38:45.600 --> 01:38:46.890
But...

01:38:54.220 --> 01:38:56.230
Come on, pick up.

01:38:56.390 --> 01:38:59.690
- Hey M.J.
- Hi. Sing your song at the beep.

01:39:00.730 --> 01:39:02.760
M.J., it's Peter. You there?

01:39:03.060 --> 01:39:05.890
Hello? You there?

01:39:06.390 --> 01:39:10.890
I'm just calling to check up on you.
Will you call me when you get in?

01:39:11.050 --> 01:39:12.470
All right, well...

01:39:12.890 --> 01:39:13.930
Don't...

01:39:14.720 --> 01:39:16.930
Don't go up any dark alleys.

01:39:17.140 --> 01:39:18.640
Hello?

01:39:21.050 --> 01:39:24.770
Can Spider-Man come out to play?

01:39:24.970 --> 01:39:26.730
Where is she?

01:40:12.930 --> 01:40:14.600
- What is that?
- That's cool!

01:40:14.810 --> 01:40:19.430
The itsy-bitsy spider
Went up the water spout

01:40:19.590 --> 01:40:23.760
Down came the goblin
And took the spider out

01:40:40.550 --> 01:40:42.300
Goblin, what have you done?

01:41:24.710 --> 01:41:28.590
Spider-Man!
This is why only fools are heroes.

01:41:28.970 --> 01:41:30.630
Because you never know...

01:41:30.790 --> 01:41:35.550
...when some lunatic will come along
with a sadistic choice:

01:41:36.670 --> 01:41:39.290
Let die the woman you love...

01:41:43.590 --> 01:41:48.670
...or suffer the little children.

01:41:51.040 --> 01:41:53.550
- Spider-Man!
- Save us!

01:41:54.050 --> 01:41:56.340
Save us!

01:41:56.630 --> 01:41:59.210
Make your choice, Spider-Man...

01:41:59.420 --> 01:42:02.800
...and see how a hero is rewarded.

01:42:02.960 --> 01:42:05.050
Don't do it, Goblin!

01:42:05.210 --> 01:42:08.120
We are who we choose to be.

01:42:08.370 --> 01:42:11.130
- Now, choose!
- No!

01:42:39.790 --> 01:42:41.380
Everybody stay still!

01:42:50.880 --> 01:42:52.170
Ahoy up there!

01:42:52.340 --> 01:42:55.290
We're gonna bring the barge
right under you.

01:43:02.790 --> 01:43:06.910
- He's coming back!
- Listen. I need you to climb down.

01:43:07.080 --> 01:43:08.580
- I can't.
- Yes, you can!

01:43:13.660 --> 01:43:16.710
M.J., you can do it. You have to.

01:43:16.870 --> 01:43:18.460
Trust me.

01:43:19.960 --> 01:43:23.790
Hold on tight and go quickly.

01:43:28.120 --> 01:43:30.170
- Hurry!
- I can't. I can't do it.

01:43:30.380 --> 01:43:32.030
Hang on, Mary Jane!

01:44:00.450 --> 01:44:03.080
- He's not gonna make it.
- He's gonna make it!

01:44:12.950 --> 01:44:16.160
It's time to die.

01:44:23.160 --> 01:44:26.990
- I got something for you!
- We ought to kick your ass!

01:44:27.150 --> 01:44:30.570
Leave Spider-Man alone!
You'd pick on a guy saving kids?

01:44:31.240 --> 01:44:34.750
You mess with Spidey,
you mess with New York!

01:44:34.910 --> 01:44:38.450
You mess with one of us,
you mess with all of us!

01:44:50.950 --> 01:44:52.740
Spider-Man, watch out!

01:45:24.570 --> 01:45:28.820
Misery, misery, misery.
That's what you've chosen.

01:45:29.740 --> 01:45:32.360
I offered you friendship...

01:45:32.530 --> 01:45:34.400
...and you spat in my face.

01:46:25.440 --> 01:46:29.110
You've spun your last web, Spider-Man.

01:46:29.270 --> 01:46:32.610
Had you not been so selfish,
your girlfriend's death...

01:46:32.780 --> 01:46:34.440
...would have been quick.

01:46:34.610 --> 01:46:38.020
But now that you've really
pissed me off...

01:46:38.270 --> 01:46:43.150
...l'm gonna finish her
nice and slow.

01:46:47.730 --> 01:46:49.770
M.J. And I...

01:46:50.610 --> 01:46:53.900
...we're gonna have a hell of a time.

01:47:47.650 --> 01:47:49.190
Peter, stop!

01:47:49.360 --> 01:47:51.810
Stop! It's me.

01:48:00.760 --> 01:48:02.270
Mr. Osborn.

01:48:02.430 --> 01:48:03.980
Thank God for you.

01:48:04.180 --> 01:48:06.520
You killed those people
on that balcony.

01:48:06.690 --> 01:48:09.720
The Goblin killed!
I had nothing to do with it!

01:48:09.890 --> 01:48:11.640
Don't let him take me again.

01:48:11.810 --> 01:48:13.850
I beg you. Protect me.

01:48:14.020 --> 01:48:17.600
You tried to kill Aunt May.
You tried to kill Mary Jane.

01:48:17.770 --> 01:48:19.260
But not you.

01:48:19.930 --> 01:48:23.890
I tried to stop it.
But I couldn't stop it.

01:48:24.100 --> 01:48:26.190
I would never hurt you.

01:48:26.390 --> 01:48:28.300
I knew from the beginning...

01:48:28.510 --> 01:48:31.430
...if anything ever happened to me...

01:48:31.600 --> 01:48:33.720
...it was you I could count on.

01:48:33.890 --> 01:48:37.260
You, Peter Parker, would save me,
and so you have.

01:48:37.840 --> 01:48:39.680
Thank God for you.

01:48:40.680 --> 01:48:42.100
Give me your hand.

01:48:43.270 --> 01:48:46.680
Believe in me
as I believed in you.

01:48:48.090 --> 01:48:50.890
I've been like a father to you.

01:48:52.430 --> 01:48:54.100
Be a son to me now.

01:48:55.880 --> 01:48:57.760
I have a father.

01:48:58.510 --> 01:49:01.010
His name was Ben Parker.

01:49:02.890 --> 01:49:04.350
Godspeed, Spider-Man.

01:49:23.260 --> 01:49:24.760
Peter.

01:49:27.090 --> 01:49:28.930
Don't tell Harry.

01:50:00.590 --> 01:50:02.300
What have you done?

01:50:02.460 --> 01:50:04.050
What have you done?!

01:50:32.170 --> 01:50:34.220
I'm so sorry, Harry.

01:50:35.130 --> 01:50:38.250
I know what it's like
to lose a father.

01:50:40.420 --> 01:50:43.720
I didn't lose him.
He was stolen from me.

01:50:45.300 --> 01:50:47.580
One day Spider-Man will pay.

01:50:49.460 --> 01:50:52.590
I swear on my father's grave,
Spider-Man will pay.

01:50:57.580 --> 01:50:59.420
Thank God for you, Peter.

01:51:00.130 --> 01:51:02.590
You're the only family I have.

01:51:27.080 --> 01:51:29.380
No matter what I do...

01:51:29.540 --> 01:51:32.670
... no matter how hard I try...

01:51:33.250 --> 01:51:37.080
... the ones I love will always
be the ones who pay.

01:51:47.790 --> 01:51:50.130
You must miss him so much.

01:51:51.090 --> 01:51:54.120
It's been so hard without him.

01:51:57.040 --> 01:51:59.920
There's something
I've been wanting to tell you.

01:52:01.700 --> 01:52:03.500
When I was up there...

01:52:04.250 --> 01:52:07.040
...and I thought I was gonna die...

01:52:08.670 --> 01:52:12.500
...there was only one person
who I was thinking of.

01:52:13.790 --> 01:52:17.000
And it wasn't who I thought it'd be.

01:52:18.460 --> 01:52:20.870
It was you, Pete.

01:52:21.740 --> 01:52:23.620
I kept thinking:

01:52:24.040 --> 01:52:26.830
"I hope I make it through this...

01:52:28.290 --> 01:52:32.660
...so I can see Peter Parker's face
one more time."

01:52:34.040 --> 01:52:35.540
Really?

01:52:35.920 --> 01:52:41.700
There's only one man
who's always been there for me...

01:52:42.950 --> 01:52:44.910
...who makes me feel...

01:52:45.370 --> 01:52:49.080
...like I'm more than I ever
thought I could be.

01:52:51.200 --> 01:52:52.870
That I'm just...

01:52:53.540 --> 01:52:55.040
...me.

01:52:56.120 --> 01:52:58.030
And that's okay.

01:53:00.240 --> 01:53:01.700
The truth is...

01:53:03.830 --> 01:53:05.620
...I love you.

01:53:07.740 --> 01:53:09.660
I love you so much, Peter.

01:53:30.370 --> 01:53:35.110
All I wanted was to tell her
how much I loved her.

01:53:35.280 --> 01:53:37.200
I can't...

01:53:39.330 --> 01:53:40.870
You can't what?

01:53:42.000 --> 01:53:43.440
Tell you...

01:53:45.160 --> 01:53:49.490
...everything.
I mean, there's so much to tell.

01:53:50.580 --> 01:53:54.490
Yeah. There's so much to tell.

01:53:55.410 --> 01:53:57.370
I want you to know...

01:53:57.780 --> 01:54:00.450
...that I will always be there
for you.

01:54:00.660 --> 01:54:04.610
I will always be there
to take care of you.

01:54:05.610 --> 01:54:07.620
I promise you that.

01:54:10.910 --> 01:54:13.190
I will always be your friend.

01:54:16.110 --> 01:54:17.990
Only a friend...

01:54:18.870 --> 01:54:20.400
...Peter Parker?

01:54:22.570 --> 01:54:25.410
That's all I have to give.

01:54:51.730 --> 01:54:54.400
Whatever life holds in store for me...

01:54:54.570 --> 01:54:57.440
...I will never forget these words:

01:54:57.650 --> 01:55:02.690
"With great power
comes great responsibility. "

01:55:02.860 --> 01:55:05.110
This is my gift.

01:55:05.280 --> 01:55:07.400
My curse.

01:55:07.900 --> 01:55:09.820
Who am I?

01:55:10.190 --> 01:55:11.570
I'm Spider-Man.
